        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Rust converters and rust removers both sit on the same hardware-store shelf and both promise to deal with rust, but they do opposite things. A converter leaves the rust where it is and chemically changes it into a stable layer you paint over. A remover dissolves or lifts the rust away so you are back to clean metal. Use a converter where you cannot reach every pit and the part will be painted anyway. Use a remover where fit, finish or function depends on bare steel.
